{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792188495,"nonce":"pvFKcEUNPKMA0hmlTNwDzsGjFRc=","message":"Fixed in 33e80ad38e61612fff98ee6c01939d5f0bb8c832. A Dynamic comparison of two closures looked only at the code pointer, so two closures over the same function with different captured values were equal and Array.remove / indexOf found the first. hlp_dyn_compare and the interpreter's dynamic_eq now follow HashLink's hl_dyn_compare: the same function over equal bound values is equal (a wrapper compares as the closure it wraps), a different function never is.\n\nChimpMonk's Repro.hx prints 'Remaining callback: 1' in interp, hybrid, jit and --preset application. New test closure_equality runs a fixture in interp, hybrid and jit against stock HashLink 1.15's output (same-object method closures equal, other-object ones not, statics, captures, Reflect.compareMethods); LLVM and Cranelift jit tiers and an AOT build give the same answers.","files":null}]}